<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · song</p><h1 class="enc-title">O Tannenbaum</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1824">1824</a>, on a folk song known from the 16th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">&quot;O Tannenbaum&quot; (&quot;O fir tree&quot;), known in English as &quot;O Christmas Tree&quot;, is a German Christmas song built on an older folk song that had nothing to do with the holiday. It draws on a long tradition in which the fir tree, green in every season, stood for faithfulness.</p></div>
